subproblems.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and H := μHE[n] on ℝ^P. Let M₁, M₂ ⊆ ℝ^P be H-null-measurable, θ₁, θ₂ : ℝ^P → ℝ, x ∈ ℝ^P, c ∈ ℝ and ρ > 0. Assume:
(i) θ₁ ≥ 0 on M₁;
(ii) θ_i is H-integrable on M_i ∩ B̄_ρ(x) for i = 1, 2;
(iii) θ₂(x) = c·θ₁(x);
(iv) for every ε > 0 and all sufficiently small s > 0, ∫⁻_{B̄_s(x)} ‖1_{M₂}θ₂ − c·1_{M₁}θ₁‖ₑ dH ≤ ofReal(ε)·∫⁻_{M₁∩B̄_s(x)} ofReal(θ₁) dH.
Then for every linear subspace Q ⊆ ℝ^P, HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M₁ θ₁ x Q implies HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M₂ θ₂ x Q.
